<XuiHtmlElement>
<Properties>
<Id>XuiHtmlElement1</Id>
<Width>544.000000</Width>
<Height>312.000000</Height>
<Position>24.000000,56.000000,0.000000</Position>
<Text>&lt;font color="#000000" size=11&gt;

&lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Images&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; can be a number of different file formats, including &lt;i&gt;.bmp&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;.png&lt;/i&gt;, and &lt;i&gt;.dds&lt;/i&gt;.
They can even be set to another &lt;i&gt;.xur&lt;/i&gt; file!
A &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Nine Grid&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; is a type of image with adjustable edge sizes, which adjusts to fit as needed.

&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;br/&gt;

There are also &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Video&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Sound&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt; controls for playing back &lt;i&gt;.wmv&lt;/i&gt; and &lt;i&gt;.wav&lt;/i&gt; files within your &lt;i&gt;&lt;b&gt;Scenes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/i&gt;.
Use them in a skin file in order to accomplish effects such as playing a sound every time a button gets focus.

&lt;/font&gt;

</Text>
</Properties>
</XuiHtmlElement>
